{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n`KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` in `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` is fail-open in a SECOND, opposite\ndirection from bug `defiable-distortive-pinniped` (ff2e): nothing validates a row against the\ntree, so a row whose helper no longer exists is kept forever with no diagnostic.\n\n**MEASURED: 4 of the 11 current rows are ghosts** — `_rebar_env`, `_env_int`, `_str_pref`,\n`_int_pref` have NO `def` site anywhere under `src/rebar`. The RP-04 config-ownership cutover\ndrained them (`269b4d5678`, `d361eb28e4`).\n\n## Why this is a real defect and not cosmetic\nA ghost row is the visible half of a rename that silently dropped keys. `269b4d5678` deleted\n`def _str_pref` and introduced `_gate_str_pref` in its place WITHOUT renaming the row. The\nresult: the row went stale (matching nothing) and `REBAR_GATE_REF` / `REBAR_GATE_SOURCE`\nsilently vanished from `docs/env-vars.md`, where they stayed missing from 2026-08-18 until\nff2e. A gate that fails when a row stops matching would have caught that rename AT the rename,\nnaming the exact cause, instead of leaving it to be found by census two months later.\n\nff2e closes the \"helper with no row\" direction (an unregistered parameter-keyed helper now\naborts the scan). This ticket is the mirror: \"row with no helper\".\n\n## Sketches (decide on evidence)\n- Fail closed on a row with no matching `def` under the scan root — symmetric with ff2e, and\n  it directly detects the rename-without-updating-the-row case.\n- Watch for the false-positive risk: a helper legitimately defined outside the scan root, or\n  a row deliberately kept for a helper about to land. If that case is real, the exemption\n  must be explicit rather than a silent skip.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` row with no matching helper definition under the scan root\n      produces a loud failure naming the stale row, proven by a test that FAILS against\n      today's generator.\n- [ ] The four ghost rows above are removed (or the gate is made to accept them with a\n      recorded, explicit reason).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the full unit sweep stay green, and\n      `docs/env-vars.md` does not shrink.\n- [ ] `scan()` keeps its 2-tuple arity — `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` unpacks it and\n      imports `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` directly, so a stricter table affects that consumer and\n      `tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py` must stay green.\n\n## Provenance\nFound by census while fixing ff2e (defiable-distortive-pinniped). Deliberately NOT folded into\nthat change: ff2e's diff is scoped to its proven root cause (helper-with-no-row), and the\nghost rows cause no key loss today, so fixing them there would have widened the diff past the\nmechanism under proof.\n\n## Fix plan (Phase 2 — authored after the RCA, scoped to the proven mechanism)\n\n**Restoration only. Validate-and-fail, nothing more.** The generator must *detect and\nrefuse*; it must never edit the table for the author. Auto-pruning a stale row, or\ninferring a row from the tree, would be a widening of behaviour rather than a restoration\nof the invariant the table already claims at `scripts/gen_env_registry.py:134`\n(\"Signatures verified against the current tree\") and that `c1f17861ec` stated as\n\"no phantom rows\".\n\n1. **Add the third fail-closed seam** to `scripts/gen_env_registry.py`: a\n   `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` row whose name has no `def`/`async def` under the shipped scan root\n   raises a distinctly-named exception naming the stale row. Distinct from\n   `UnrecognisedEnvironAccess` and `UnregisteredEnvReadHelper`, per the module's own\n   convention of keeping each seam separately diagnosable. All stale rows are reported at\n   once, matching `_raise_for_environ` / `_raise_for_helpers`.\n2. **Root-independent by design, and documented as such.** The check validates the table\n   against `DEFAULT_SCAN_ROOT` — the shipped `src/rebar` surface the table describes — and\n   never against the caller's `root`. Measured reason: against a one-module synthetic tree\n   (the `_scan_source` fixture used at 11 sites in `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`)\n   **13 of 13** rows are ghosts, so a root-scoped check is a false-positive storm. This\n   mirrors two existing precedents in the sibling gate — `_check_registry_completeness()`\n   and `_validate_exceptions()`, the latter documented as \"Root-independent structural\n   validation\". The scoping is recorded in the code, not left as a silent skip.\n3. **Remove the four ghost rows** `_rebar_env`, `_env_int`, `_str_pref`, `_int_pref`.\n   Measured effect: 122 -> 122 keys (nothing lost), one corrected line in the artifact.\n4. **Re-point `tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py:96`**, whose fixture\n   selects a helper via `next(iter(KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS))` and implicitly assumes argument\n   position 0. It goes RED on ghost removal (measured: `assert 0 == 1` at `:99`). Re-point\n   it to build the call from the row's *declared* `(pos, prefix)` so it stops depending on\n   dict insertion order — strictly stronger, no assertion removed or weakened.\n5. **Regenerate `docs/env-vars.md`** in the same commit.\n\n**Gates before push:** `make lint` (incl. the shrink-only complexity ratchet at\n`new=0 increased=0 stale=0`), `make typecheck`, the full unit sweep, plus the two oracles\nthis area has already bitten changes on — `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and\n`tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py`.\n\n**Not in scope (and deliberately so):** auto-pruning or auto-inferring rows; changing\n`scan()`'s 2-tuple arity (`check_config_ownership.py` unpacks it); widening the ownership\ngate; fixing the `prefix` field's now-total absence of live coverage (`_rebar_env` was its\nonly user — noted as residual risk, not repaired here)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787310530597969001,"uuid":"ae6f12f7-7164-4670-a071-34e1730d66f5"}